 shift in the national House environment toward Republicans could pull this toward Lean D territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Susie Lee (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Susie Lee seeks another term in a Las Vegas-area district that leans Democratic by only about a point, making this one of the more competitive House seats on paper. She enters the fall with a fundraising edge over Republican Marty O'Donnell, who has raised a substantial sum himself and has drawn national attention with appearances at Republican midterm events. Independent candidates trail far behind in money.\n\nExpert raters split between Lean D and Safe D, averaging out to Likely D, and prediction markets give Lee roughly a 92% chance of winning. With no public general-election polls available, the race rests on fundamentals, which point to a Democratic margin in the high single digits.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9366, "margin": 9.91}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9036, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9329, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9282, "margin": 9.5}]}